  "findings": [
    "Paired wheel/pinion views reproduce the two roller banks between the drive rims, central chain sprocket and independent shaft supports shown in SNL25. Casting webs and transitions remain visibly simplified.",
    "The section exposes separate bushings, counterbores, shaft shoulders and axial oil gallery. HB81 supports the arrangement; exact casting profiles, thread forms and hydraulic operation remain unqualified.",
    "The standard view shows both rear bearing caps per side. Sponson fittings, exterior hardware and most machinery remain unfinished; existing layout envelopes stay visible.",
    "Receiver and hull underside views show the pinion drilling and continuous fuel enclosure. The fuel backplate station is an explicit geometric correction supported by a separate native neighbor study; its historical station is not measured by HB27.",
    "Cotters remain unsplayed supplied-length approximations. The 35/37 driving-tooth conflict and continuous gearing remain open.",
    "Chain interface is not qualified in this nominal casting: the separate HB130-sized roller study found that its provisional 22.525 mm circular pockets are too small. A separate repeated-flank candidate is being tested and has not changed this model."
  ]
